      "role": "user",
      "content": "# JCROWN DIGITALS — PREMIUM BLACK & GOLD PERSONAL BRAND WEBSITE\n\nAct as a senior UI/UX designer, personal-brand copywriter, and full-stack web developer. Build a beautiful, modern, fully functional personal-brand landing page for **JCROWN DIGITALS**, owned by **Jediah Akeredolu**.\n\nThis website should focus on Jediah as the person behind the brand, his work, his digital books, and the value visitors can get from his publications. It should not look like a traditional e-commerce store.\n\n## 1. Brand identity\n\n**Brand:** JCROWN DIGITALS  \n**Owner:** Jediah Akeredolu  \n**Brand colours:** Premium black and gold.\n\nUse:\n- Deep black for the main background and prominent sections.\n- Elegant gold for important headings, buttons, borders, and accents.\n- White and soft ivory for readable body text.\n- Subtle charcoal panels for secondary sections.\n\nUse refined typography, beautiful spacing, subtle transitions, and professional book-cover mockups. Gold should feel luxurious, not excessively bright or overpowering.\n\nThe website should feel premium, confident, intelligent, personal, and trustworthy.\n\n## 2. Homepage structure\n\n### Section 1: Navigation\n\nCreate a clean header with the JCROWN DIGITALS wordmark and these navigation links:\n\n- Home\n- About Jediah\n- My Books\n- Free Resources\n- Contact\n\nUse smooth scrolling to the relevant sections. The mobile navigation must also work correctly.\n\n### Section 2: Hero introduction\n\nCreate a striking first screen with a black background, elegant gold typography, and a portrait placeholder for Jediah Akeredolu.\n\nDisplay:\n\n**JCROWN DIGITALS**\n\n**Welcome to the World of Jediah Akeredolu**\n\n\"Discover my world of ideas, digital publications, and resources created to share knowledge, inspire growth, and make useful information accessible.\"\n\nInclude a subtle visual of digital books or an elegant stack of eBook covers.\n\nKeep the hero clean and uncluttered. The main focus should be Jediah and his brand.\n\n### Section 3: About Jediah Akeredolu\n\nWrite a compelling, professional introduction that presents Jediah as the creator behind JCROWN DIGITALS.\n\nUse this draft as the starting point:\n\n**Meet Jediah Akeredolu**\n\n\"Jediah Akeredolu is the person behind JCROWN DIGITALS, a digital platform created to share ideas, publications, and valuable resources with readers. Through his work, he aims to make knowledge easier to access and give people an opportunity to discover useful perspectives and information through digital content.\n\nJCROWN DIGITALS represents his commitment to bringing his work together in one accessible space, where readers can explore his publications, discover available resources, and stay informed about new releases.\n\nWhether you are visiting to discover a book, explore a free resource, or learn more about his work, JCROWN DIGITALS is designed to make that experience simple, welcoming, and accessible.\"\n\nThis is provisional brand copy, not a verified biography. Do not invent Jediah's age, qualifications, career history, personal experiences, achievements, or other facts. Allow him to edit this introduction when he provides more information about himself.\n\nUse a professional portrait placeholder, elegant layout, and readable typography.\n\n### Section 4: What JCROWN DIGITALS offers\n\nIntroduce the platform's main purpose with a short heading:\n\n**Knowledge Worth Discovering**\n\nExplain that visitors can explore Jediah's digital books and access available resources through the website.\n\nInclude three elegant visual features:\n- **Digital Publications** — Explore books published by Jediah.\n- **Free Resources** — Access publications and resources specifically made available for free.\n- **New Releases & Updates** — Stay informed about new books and other updates.\n\nThese features should use simple icons or tasteful visual elements rather than large, distracting illustrations.\n\nOnly advertise resources and services that are actually available.\n\n### Section 5: The main call-to-action button\n\nImmediately after the introductory writing and brand-information sections, place one prominent gold button with the exact label:\n\n**DOWNLOAD BOOKS HERE**\n\nThis button is extremely important.\n\nWhen a visitor clicks it, the website must smoothly scroll directly to the eBook download section further down the same homepage.\n\nImplementation requirements:\n- Give the eBook section the HTML ID `books`.\n- Link the button to `#books`.\n- Enable smooth scrolling.\n- Account for a fixed header so the section heading is not hidden.\n- Make the button accessible by keyboard.\n- Provide a visible hover and focus state.\n- Make it work on mobile and desktop.\n\nDo not make this button open an unrelated page, require registration, or do nothing.\n\nThe button must appear after the introductory and About Jediah content, as requested.\n\n### Section 6: Book download section\n\nCreate a visually impressive section with the ID `books`.\n\nHeading:\n\n**Explore & Download My Books**\n\nSupporting text:\n\n\"Discover the publications available through JCROWN DIGITALS. Choose a book to view its details and access the available download.\"\n\nDisplay books in a clean, responsive grid of elegant cards.\n\nEach book card should contain:\n- Book cover.\n- Book title.\n- Short description.\n- Author name where appropriate.\n- File format.\n- A clear FREE or price label.\n- A functional action button.\n\nFor free books, the button should say **Download Book** or **Download Free**.\n\nFor paid books, the button should say **Get This Book** and open a real checkout flow. Never provide paid files before payment has been verified.\n\nThe owner must be able to upload books, covers, descriptions, and files from the admin portal.\n\n**Visitors must be able to download free books without signing up, logging in, or submitting their email address.**\n\nOnly show books that have actually been uploaded and published. If there are no books yet, show a polished message such as \"New publications are coming soon\" rather than fake books or invented download links.\n\n### Section 7: Stay connected\n\nCreate a simple black-and-gold subscription section.\n\nHeading:\n\n**Stay Connected with JCROWN DIGITALS**\n\nSupporting text:\n\n\"Get updates when new books, publications, and resources become available.\"\n\nInclude an email field and a gold **Subscribe for Updates** button.\n\nSubscription must be optional. Visitors must still be able to browse and download free books without subscribing.\n\nConnect the form to a real backend and email service. Validate the email, show an accurate success or error message, and include an unsubscribe link in marketing emails.\n\n### Section 8: Contact Jediah\n\nCreate a clean contact section with:\n- Name.\n- Email.\n- Subject.\n- Message.\n- Send Message button.\n\nSave submitted enquiries in the admin portal and display a confirmation only after successful submission.\n\nInclude social media and contact links only when Jediah supplies the actual details.\n\n### Section 9: Footer\n\nCreate a minimal black footer with gold accents.\n\nInclude:\n- JCROWN DIGITALS.\n- Jediah Akeredolu.\n- Home.\n- About.\n- Books.\n- Contact.\n- Privacy Policy.\n- Terms and Conditions.\n- Configured social links.\n- Copyright notice.\n\nThe Books link must also scroll to the `#books` section.\n\n## 3. Secure admin portal\n\nBuild a separate admin portal at `/admin`, protected by proper authentication.\n\nJediah must be able to:\n- Add, edit, upload, and publish books.\n- Upload book covers and digital files.\n- Mark books free or paid.\n- Update his biography and portrait.\n- Edit all homepage text.\n- Manage contact information and social links.\n- Publish announcements.\n- Manage notification subscribers and unsubscribe requests.\n- Read contact-form messages.\n- View download statistics.\n- Manage paid orders if paid publications are enabled.\n\nChanges made in the admin portal must appear on the public website after saving and publishing.\n\nUse secure file storage, server-side permissions, input validation, and safe authentication. Never expose administrator credentials or payment secrets in the frontend.\n\n## 4. Every button must work\n\nAudit every interactive element before delivery.\n\n- Home → scrolls to the top.\n- About Jediah → scrolls to the About section.\n- My Books → scrolls to `#books`.\n- **DOWNLOAD BOOKS HERE** → scrolls directly to `#books`.\n- Download Free → downloads the correct published free file.\n- Get This Book → opens the actual paid-product checkout.\n- Subscribe for Updates → submits the subscription to the backend.\n- Send Message → submits and stores the contact enquiry.\n- Admin Login → authenticates the administrator.\n- Save Changes → persists the updated content.\n- Upload Book → validates and stores the file.\n- Publish Book → makes the approved publication available publicly.\n\nNo decorative buttons, empty links, fake forms, or hard-coded success messages.\n\nIf a feature requires an external service that has not been configured, explain what is missing instead of pretending the feature works.\n\n## 5. Technical and quality requirements\n\nUse the existing project stack if one is already available. Otherwise, choose a modern, maintainable stack suitable for the environment.\n\nImplement:\n- Responsive layouts.\n- Secure admin authentication.\n- A real database.\n- Secure file uploads and downloads.\n- Functional forms and navigation.\n- Server-side validation.\n- Proper error handling.\n- Accessibility and keyboard navigation.\n- SEO metadata.\n- Fast page loading.\n- Clear setup and deployment instructions.\n\nPreserve the personal-brand landing-page experience. Do not turn the design into a complicated e-commerce marketplace.\n\n## Final instruction\n\nThe website should tell visitors who Jediah Akeredolu is, explain the purpose of JCROWN DIGITALS, present his work beautifully, and then guide visitors to the books.\n\nThe primary visitor journey should be:\n\n**Discover JCrown → Learn about Jediah → Click DOWNLOAD BOOKS HERE → Browse and download available books.**\n\nKeep the design premium, black and gold, simple to navigate, and fully functional.        FIX IT NA AND MAKE IT BETTER"
    },
